user":{"login":"ej-sanmartin","id":29460583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDYwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29460583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin","html_url":"https://github.com/ej-sanmartin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T03:51:28Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T03:51:28Z","body":"A hunch but looks like de-serialization / translating the editor enum is happenning on project open and NOT on Godot startup. I'll investigate this as well and see if this is the issue or something else.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698232942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698235525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113994#issuecomment-3698235525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113994","id":3698235525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cbpiF","user":{"login":"ej-sanmartin","id":29460583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDYwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29460583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin","html_url":"https://github.com/ej-sanmartin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T03:53:06Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T03:54:05Z","body":"Oh wait, just re-read @YeldhamDev comment, this is a bit deeper than just the editor enums then. BUT probably a timing issue of all C#-defined enums.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698235525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698334846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113994#issuecomment-3698334846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113994","id":3698334846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ccBx-","user":{"login":"ej-sanmartin","id":29460583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDYwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29460583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin","html_url":"https://github.com/ej-sanmartin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ej-sanmartin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T05:15:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T05:43:38Z","body":"Okay so these settings are registered with `PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM` in `GodotSharpEditor._EnterTree()`, which only runs when a project is opened. In the Project Manager, EditorNode is never created, so GodotTools never loads and the hints are never registered.\n\nThere's two approaches we can go with though I need a Godot maintainer's recommendation.\n\n## Proposals\n\n### 1. Load GodotTools.dll in Project Manager and call a settings-only registration method\n\n**Pros:**\n- Minimal C++ changes, most work in C# (thus more ownership for the dotnet team)\n- Uses existing plugin loading infrastructure\n\n**Cons:**\n- GodotTools must handle \"partially loaded\" state (actually not too bad, just ensure loading logic is on C++ side, remove from C#)\n- Loads managed assembly in Project Manager (slight startup overhead)\n- Needs graceful degradation if assembly fails to load\n\n---\n\n### 2. Add C++ -> C# Callback for Settings\n\n**Pros:**\n- Clean API boundary (C# provides data, C++ consumes)\n- No assembly loading overhead in Project Manager\n\n**Cons:**\n- More C++ complexity\n- New callback type in managed callbacks infrastructure\n- Must verify callback availability timing\n\n---\n\n**Question for maintainers:** Which approach better fits Godot's architecture and maintenance goals?\n\nFirst option is pragmatic and makes the most sense conceptually (\"just have these C# settings load earlier\"). But the potential performance overhead is somewhat a dealbreaker for me from just settings.\n\n~~I'm leaning the latter since it doesn't require loading an entire assembly just to register settings, though it's a more complex.~~\n\n*EDIT:* I've changed my mind, latter may be a bit too envasive and complex for this use case, though still want to hear what you think.\n\nA *third* option (which I didn't like) is we hard code in C++ on project start with what these enum hints should be. I didn't like it because then we'd have two places where these enums would be defined and we'd have to ensure these don't become inconsistent. It would be easiest though.\n\nPlus I think these enum names are dynamically generated, which can introduce some complexity/ambiguity in C++ impl of this:\n\n`modules/mono/editor/GodotTools/GodotTools/GodotSharpEditor.cs:569-577`\n```cs\n    // For example, for macOS platform\n    else if (OS.IsMacOS)\n    {\n        settingsHintStr += $\",Visual Studio:{(int)ExternalEditorId.VisualStudioForMac}\" +\n                           $\",MonoDevelop:{(int)ExternalEditorId.MonoDevelop}\" +\n                           $\",Visual Studio Code and VSCodium:{(int)ExternalEditorId.VsCode}\" +\n                           $\",JetBrains Rider:{(int)ExternalEditorId.Rider}\" +\n                           $\",JetBrains Fleet:{(int)ExternalEditorId.Fleet}\" +\n                           $\",Custom:{(int)ExternalEditorId.CustomEditor}\";\n   }\n```\n\nlmk what's preferred.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698334846/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710307958","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113994#issuecomment-3710307958","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113994","id":3710307958,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dJs52","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T12:55:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T12:55:38Z","body":"CC @raulsntos \n\nI think the most pragramatic approach here would be to define these settings in C++ (e.g. in `register_types.cpp` or wherever appropriate) so we don't need to initialize a C# runtime to get their value in the Project Manager.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710307958/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711617225","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113994#issuecomment-3711617225","issue_url":"https://ap